!ReelEGL - Reel, drawing through EGL (an example)       0.1.14
===================================================================

ReelEGL is the Reel video player built a second way: the picture goes
through riscos-mesa's EGL instead of Reel's own sprite plotting. It is
here as a working example of an EGL program (riscos-ffmpeg's ffegl
library, ffegl_draw_surface, on the reelcore player core that Reel uses
too), and to compare the two. Everything else - the
controls, keys, menus, sound - is the same as Reel: see !Reel's !Help.
Both can run at once (they have different icon bar icons: ReelEGL's
reel has a green hub).

How it draws
------------
- In the window, the picture is an EGL "work area surface": a surface
  of fixed size at the top of the window's work area, under which the
  controls are ordinary Wimp icons. Each frame is converted by swscale
  straight into the surface (EGL_KHR_lock_surface) and eglSwapBuffers
  shows it; redraws plot it with eglPlotSurfaceRISCOS.
- Full screen uses EGL's whole-screen surface. With Vsync (full screen)
  ticked (the window menu; the default) EGL plots each picture after
  waiting for the screen's refresh (eglSwapInterval 1): no tearing.
  Untick it and frames go straight into screen memory
  (EGL_SINGLE_BUFFER): no plot at all, the fastest way, but you may see
  tearing. *Set ReelEGL$NoVsync 1 starts with it off.
- The mini player (M) is a second window; its picture is a work area
  surface of its own, made when it opens (only one surface exists at a
  time, so switching makes the other window's surface again).

Needs
-----
As Reel. The EGL and OpenGL libraries are built in (from riscos-mesa
20.3.5-7pre12); no modules are needed for them.

